Hi all,

Hello from the future - I was interested in the question when it was posted a couple years ago and talked with Tiago about it just last month.

Although this may be too late to be of primary interest, these's a solution that I think is more efficient than an inverse variance-weighted average. A weighted average that achieves a smaller variance takes into account the correlation of the two estimators and uses the full covariance matrix; see https://www.numdam.org/item/JSFS_2017__158_3_106_0.pdf in particular eq. (3) and the display at the top of the same page. The full covariance matrix can be estimated with a bootstrap (or with influence functions, see e.g. https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.12439).

Best wishes,
Ben

